SECTION claim-evidence
NUMBER 5.2
TITLE "Claim-level evidence — `12-CLAIM-EVIDENCE.md`"

GOAL
  Every claim record binds its subject, field or step, evidence level, anchor, and
  lineage so that materiality and projection classification are explicit.
END

FIELD CLAIM
  subject-id-record-version    -> string                                  required
  field-step                   -> string                                  required
  claim                        -> string                                  required
  materiality                  -> REGISTRY-CLAIM-MATERIALITY              required
  evidence-level               -> REGISTRY-CLAIM-EVIDENCE-LEVEL           required
  anchor                       -> string                                  required
  source-fingerprint-snapshot  -> string                                  required
  evidence-route-lineage-id    -> string                                  required
  projection-classification    -> REGISTRY-CLAIM-PROJECTION-CLASSIFICATION required
  independent-supporting-claims -> set<string>                            optional
  independence-basis           -> string                                  required
  contradiction-ids            -> set<string>                             optional
  created-last-revalidated-by  -> string                                  required
END

FIELD BLOCK-EVIDENCE-SUMMARY
  block-confidence-rank  -> REGISTRY-ATOMICCOMPONENT-BLOCK-CONFIDENCE-RANK required
  block-evidence-profile -> string                                          required
END

SECTION sanitized-projections
NUMBER 5.3
TITLE "Sanitized projections and helper limitations"

GOAL
  A sanitized export produced by an approved local helper is an agent-visible
  evidence projection.
END

RULE sanitized-projections-rules
  GOAL
    The projection MUST include raw-source fingerprint lineage and a sanitization
    report classifying preserved, normalized, aliased, redacted, removed, and
    unclassified content. E-DIRECT is permitted only for preserved or
    semantics-preservingly normalized behavior. Aliases prove reference existence,
    not secret value, connectivity, authorization, or runtime validity. Behavior
    dependent on redacted, removed, or unclassified content remains E-INFERRED or
    E-UNKNOWN and creates a ticket when material. Entity-correlation output is a
    candidate-discovery aid only. It MUST NOT become evidence, a call edge,
    ownership proof, or automatic inclusion without a direct structural signal or
    explicit human scope decision. Private matching hints and private entity-usage
    indexes MUST NOT enter agent-visible inventory.
  END
END

SECTION contradictions
NUMBER 5.4
TITLE "Contradictions — `14-CONTRADICTIONS.md`"

GOAL
  Every contradiction record names the conflicting claims, scope, and stale impact.
END

FIELD CONTRADICTION
  claims-in-conflict             -> set<string> required
  scope-environments-snapshots   -> string       required
  conflict-description           -> string       required
  resolution-state               -> REGISTRY-CONTRADICTION-RESOLUTION-STATE required
  resolution-decision-id         -> string       optional
  affected-records-and-stale-impact -> string    required
END

SECTION authoritative-decisions
NUMBER 5.5
TITLE "Authoritative decisions — `15-DECISIONS.md`"

GOAL
  Every decision record carries its content version and fingerprint, exact scope and
  denominator effect, approval status, and approval envelope bindings.
END

FIELD DECISION
  decision-content-version                          -> int required
  decision-content-fingerprint                      -> hash required
  type                                              -> REGISTRY-DECISION-TYPE required
  observed-inputs                                   -> string required
  options-decision-rationale-risks                  -> string required
  exact-scope-and-denominator-effect                -> string required
  affected-records-rollout-rollback                 -> string required
  content-supersession                              -> string required
  approval-status                                   -> REGISTRY-DECISION-APPROVAL-STATUS required
  approval-envelope-version                         -> int required
  owner-approver-authority-basis-approval-timestamp -> string required
  approved-content-binding                          -> string required
  approval-signature-audit                          -> string required
END

SECTION acquisition-candidates
NUMBER 5.6
TITLE "Acquisition-candidate reconciliation — `17-ACQUISITION-CANDIDATES.md`"

GOAL
  Every helper-published candidate and operator action receives a row in
  17-ACQUISITION-CANDIDATES.md and a deterministic CND ID whose canonical key binds
  the stable candidate or action identity, helper policy version, and pinned snapshot.
END

RULE candidate-reconciliation
  GOAL
    Duplicate candidate or action identities and reused CND IDs are invalid. States
    are Included, Rejected-With-Operator-Decision, Approved-Excluded, or Pending. The
    helper manifest MUST attest that all accessible workflow metadata was scanned for
    the pinned snapshot, all direct structural matches were included, all
    high-confidence entity-only matches were human-reviewed, and all configured
    medium-confidence candidates received an operator decision; scoring thresholds
    and policy versions are recorded. Lower-confidence omissions follow the
    configured, approved scope policy. Helper publication completeness means safe
    approved outputs were produced; protocol A-STRUCTURALLY-COMPLETE additionally
    requires every candidate, operator action, and dynamic reference row terminal.
    Correlation remains discovery and scope input only, never behavioral evidence or
    an automatic edge.
  END
END

SECTION human-confirmations
NUMBER 5.7
TITLE "Human confirmations — `18-CONFIRMATIONS.md`"

GOAL
  A CNF record confirms exact typed record IDs, semantic versions, and fingerprints
  against a pinned closed snapshot, never mutable whole-file bytes.
END

FIELD CONFIRMATION
  human-hatch-action                                -> REGISTRY-CONFIRMATION-HUMAN-HATCH-ACTION required
  approver-role-authority-basis                     -> string required
  review-timestamp-review-scope-limitations         -> string required
  handbook-readability-review                       -> REGISTRY-CONFIRMATION-HANDBOOK-READABILITY-REVIEW required
  confirmed-record-bindings                         -> set<string> required
  pinned-exit-a-exit-e-candidate-report-candidate-payload-manifest-fingerprints -> string required
  required-dec-content-versions-fingerprints-and-approval-envelopes-reviewed -> string required
  invalidated-by                                    -> REGISTRY-CONFIRMATION-INVALIDATED-BY required
  cnf-signature-envelope-version                    -> int required
  cnf-payload-fingerprint                           -> hash required
  signature-or-approval-reference-signature-timestamp -> string required
END
